OVERRIDES.update({
    'LayoutDialog.Run': 'Shows the dialog and blocks until it is closed; returns `DialogResult.Ok` or `DialogResult.Cancel`, or `DialogResult.None_` when the dialog was already run or its layout is not valid. `helpID` is the contextual help identifier.',
    'class:LayoutDialog': [
        'Modal layout manager dialog, built control by control in code. Life cycle (one-shot: a dialog runs at most once):',
        '1. **Construct** — the layout is created with its OK and (optional) Cancel button.\n'
        '2. **Add controls** — `Add<Control>(controlID, ...)` for every control. IDs are chosen by the caller (3 .. 9999).\n'
        '3. **Position controls** — `SetFirstItem(controlID)` for the top-left control, then `PlaceBelow` / `PlaceRight` relative to another control. Children of a group box, tab pane or swap pane start with `SetFirstGroupItem(groupControlID, controlID)`. `BindEdges` and `Align*` control resizing.\n'
        '4. **Register handlers** — `OnSetup`, `OnControl(controlID, handler)`, `OnOk`, `OnCancel`, ... (all optional; handlers are Python callables receiving a `DialogEvent`).\n'
        '5. **Run** — shows the dialog and blocks until it is closed; returns `DialogResult.Ok` or `DialogResult.Cancel`.\n'
        '6. **Read values** — the `Get...` functions keep working after `Run`: the values of all controls are captured when the dialog closes.',
        'Value functions (`Set...`, `Select...`, `Add...Item`, ...) may be called at any time after the control was added; calls made before the dialog is shown are queued and applied, in order, right before the Setup handler runs. `Get...` functions return `None` before the dialog is shown.',
        'Indices of choices, list browser rows/columns and tab panes are 0-based. Tree items are identified by the ID returned from `AddTreeItem`; the root parent is -1. `controlID`, `referenceControlID`, `groupControlID`, `paneControlID`, `tabControlID` and `swapControlID` identify controls; `alignmentGroupID` is a shared edge-alignment identifier, not a control; `itemID` and `parentID` identify items within a tree control.',
    ],
})
